Comment:
 The third_party/ tree contains vendored upstream dependencies.  Each
 component retains its own copyright and license terms as recorded in
 the LICENSE file inside its respective subdirectory, which is shipped
 unchanged in the source package and reproduced verbatim in
 /usr/share/doc/libduckdb-dev/third_party-licenses/.
 .
 Components that do not currently ship an in-tree LICENSE file in
 this snapshot are: catch, imdb, thrift.  Their license terms are
 those of the respective upstream projects (Catch2 / Boost Software
 License 1.0; Apache Thrift / Apache-2.0; IMDb-derived benchmark
 schema / Expat-equivalent permissive terms per the DuckDB project)
 but the canonical text is not vendored in this tree.  Downstream
 redistributors who require a complete, in-tree LICENSE record for
 these components should verify with upstream before further
 redistribution.

